<blockquote>
<p>I kind of don't see why this is here? It's like, it makes you randomly terrified?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This one actually has a bit of real science behind it; people who spend prolonged periods amid unshielded and variable EM fields tend to display symptoms of paranoia, nervousness, and even mild hallucinations. This usually only ends up happening in enclosed areas (i.e. a closet with a large improperly shielded circuit breaker, a very small room with entirely too many computer systems, etc.) and usually amongst people with a certain sensitivity to it, but it's been known to happen in some larger areas from time to time. The fact that this place causes electrical malfunctions when the events happen actually plays along with it.</p>
